{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And they spoke to him all the words of Joseph which he had spoken to them.</b> The Ramban, z\"l, wrote: this refers to what they told him — 'Thus says your son Joseph: Elohim has set me,' etc. — and that the Holy One, blessed be He, had sent him to sustain them and to provide for his father and his brothers. And when it says 'all the words of Joseph,' this does not include their telling him what he said to them: 'for you sold me hither,' etc., for our father Jacob never knew this; rather he thought that he had wandered in the field and those who found him took him and sold him to Egypt. And they did not tell him, for they would not tell their own sin, and furthermore because they feared lest he curse them as he did to Reuben, and also to Simeon and Levi; and Joseph too, in his modesty and humility, did not tell his father. And the proof that he never knew this is the verse that says (Genesis 49): 'And they charged Joseph, saying: Your father commanded before his death, saying: I pray you, forgive,' etc. — and had Jacob known the matter, it would have been fitting for them to entreat their father's face to command Joseph to forgive them, and he would surely honor his face and not disobey his word, and they would not need to fabricate matters from their own heart." "<b>And the spirit of Jacob their father revived.</b> Onkelos translated: 'and the spirit of prophecy rested upon him,' because he could have said 'and Jacob their father lived,' but since he added the word רוח (spirit), he translated it as the spirit of prophecy."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:34.609696236Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}